.TH STORMBYTE-GITHUB 1 "August 2026" "StormByte-GitHub 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-GitHub \- unified CLI for GitHub Actions caches, CI runs, git ops, pin-aware submodules, dumps, releases, forks and sanitizer tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-GitHub
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-GitHub
is a Bash CLI for day-to-day work across many local GitHub clones under one
working root.
It wraps
.BR gh (1)
and
.BR git (1)
for Actions caches, workflow runs, git reset/pull, first-level submodule
re-pinning, source dumps, GitHub Releases, fork sync, code search, clone-all
and AddressSanitizer / ThreadSanitizer test builds.
.PP
Version
.BR 1.1.0
requires
.B StormByte-functions-bash
\(>= 1.3.0
.RI ( functions.sh )
and
.B StormByte-functions-git
\(>= 1.3.0
.RI ( git.sh ).
.PP
A configuration file
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
is mandatory and must contain at least
.BR OWNER ,
.BR ROOT
and
.BR OUT .
.B FORK_ROOT
is optional.
If the file is missing on first run, the script prompts interactively
(with path completion where applicable), validates the answers and writes
the file.
Empty optional values such as
.B FORK_ROOT
are omitted from the file.
.PP
Invoking the program with no arguments, or with
.BR help ,
prints the built-in help and exits 0.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
Configuration file. Supported variables:
.RS
.TP
.B OWNER
GitHub username that owns the repositories.
Used to verify origin remotes and by
.BR clone-all .
.TP
.B ROOT
Working root that contains local clones.
Used by most commands when no path is given, and by
.BR "repos list" .
.TP
.B OUT
Output directory for
.B repos dump
(created automatically if missing).
.TP
.B FORK_ROOT
Optional root used
.B only
by the
.B fork
commands.
If unset, fork uses
.BR ROOT .
.RE
.SH GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
Any configuration value can be overridden for a single run:
.TP
.B DRY_RUN=1
Simulate actions without applying them
(checkouts, deletes, commits, pushes, clones, ...).
.TP
.B ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B ROOT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B OUT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B OUT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B OWNER=\fIname\fR
Override
.B OWNER
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B FORK_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B FORK_ROOT
from the config file for this run.
.TP
.B PAGE_LIMIT=\fIN\fR
Items per API page (default: 100).
.TP
.B MAX_PAGES=\fIN\fR
Maximum number of cache-delete passes (0 = until empty).
.TP
.B RUN_LIMIT=\fIN\fR
Maximum number of workflows to re-run (0 = all).
.TP
.B ONLY_FAILED=1
Legacy equivalent of
.BR --failed .
.SH DIRECTORY SELECTION
Most commands accept an optional
.IR dir-spec .
The argument is always a
.B local directory
(clone path), never the GitHub repository name.
.TP
(no argument)
Every immediate subdirectory of the effective root
.RB ( ROOT
for most commands;
.B FORK_ROOT
or
.B ROOT
for
.BR fork ).
.TP
.B <dir>
That directory only.
May be absolute, relative,
.BR ~/... ,
or a simple name resolved as
.IR <root>/<name> .
.TP
.B !<name>
All directories under the effective root except that basename.
.TP
.B !<name1>+!<name2>+...
Exclude several basenames.
.PP
Notes:
.IP \(bu 2
A concrete path (~/..., /..., ./..., foo/bar) is used as-is.
.IP \(bu 2
A simple name is resolved as
.IR <root>/<name> .
.IP \(bu 2
The walk is
.B not
recursive: only immediate children of the effective root.
.IP \(bu 2
When using
.B !
exclusions from an interactive shell, quote them
(e.g.
.BR "'!multimedia'" )
so Bash history expansion does not consume the mark.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS help
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in help message and exit.
.SS cache
.TP
.B cache show\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
List each Actions cache (id, size, key) per repository together with totals.
With
.B --name
only keys matching the bash glob are shown.
.TP
.B cache list\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
Compact count and size per repository.
With
.B --name
only matching keys are counted.
.TP
.B cache delete\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--name\fR \fIpattern\fR]
Delete Actions caches, paging the API until empty
(or until
.BR MAX_PAGES ).
With
.B --name
only matching keys are deleted, and paging stops when a page has no matches.
Respects
.BR DRY_RUN .
.PP
.B --name
uses bash glob syntax
(e.g.
.BR '*ccache*' ,
.BR 'sccache-Windows-*' ).
The flag may appear anywhere after the subcommand.
.SS ci
.TP
.B ci stop\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Cancel unique active workflow runs
.RB ( in_progress ,
.BR queued ,
.BR pending ,
.BR waiting ,
.BR requested )
on the current branch.
.TP
.B ci start\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--failed\fR]
Re-run the latest finished run of each workflow
(deduplicated by workflow name).
With
.B --failed
only
.BR failure ,
.BR cancelled ,
.B timed_out
and
.B startup_failure
runs are re-launched.
Already-active workflows are skipped.
.TP
.B ci restart\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--failed\fR]
.B ci stop
, a short pause, then
.BR "ci start" .
.TP
.B ci status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Recent runs on the current branch
(STATUS, CONCLUSION, WORKFLOW, TITLE).
.SS submodules
.TP
.B submodules init\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
.B git submodule update --init --recursive
.
.TP
.B submodules deinit\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
.B git submodule deinit --all -f
.
.TP
.B submodules list\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Print name, path and URL from
.IR .gitmodules
(or
.RI `` none '').
.TP
.B submodules update\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fB--confirm\fR]
Re-pin
.B first-level
modules only.
Nested modules are then synced to the SHAs the parent has just staged.
When no directory is given, parents under
.B ROOT
are walked in dependency order
(Kahn topological sort over
.I .gitmodules
URLs that resolve to other clones under
.BR ROOT ).
.sp
Policy (parent
.I .gitmodules
.B branch=
plus the module checkout), implemented via
.B git_sm_plan
in
.IR git.sh :
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B A
.RI ( branch=master ):
float to
.BR origin/master .
Already at that SHA \(->
.IR "No changes" .
.IP \(bu 2
.B B1
(no master; checkout is a recognised release tag):
jump to the
.B latest
tag in the same family
(same prefix and grain).
Same tag, different SHA \(-> re-release.
.IP \(bu 2
.B B2
(no master; checkout is
.B not
a tag, e.g.
.B branch=master
was removed):
pin the latest tag of the inferred family.
A downgrade is intentional.
If no family can be inferred, the newest recognised release.
.IP \(bu 2
Unrecognised pins \(->
.BR UNRESOLVED .
On a TTY the user may type a ref.
Under
.B --confirm
or a non-TTY those rows are skipped.
.RE
.sp
Recognised families (tables live in
.IR git.sh ,
append-only):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
own libraries:
.BR X.Y
/
.BR X.Y.Z
.IP \(bu 2
PostgreSQL:
.B REL_16_4
\(-> 16.4, family by major
.RB ( REL_16_* )
.IP \(bu 2
Crypto++:
.B CRYPTOPP_8_9_0
\(-> 8.9.0, family by
.B X.Y
while the prefix matches
.RE
.sp
Before any checkout:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
If the parent worktree is dirty it is stashed
.RI ( "StormByte-GitHub auto-stash before submodules update" )
and restored at the end.
A conflicted
.B stash pop
leaves the stash in place.
.IP \(bu 2
A table is printed:
.BR MODULE ,
.BR CURRENT ,
.BR PLANNED .
.IR "No changes"
is dark green; updates are light green; unresolved / errors are red.
.IP \(bu 2
On a TTY, without
.BR --confirm ,
and if there is work, the script asks
.BR [y/N]
via
.BR confirm_yes .
.B --confirm
or a non-TTY applies the plan without prompting.
.B DRY_RUN=1
prints the plan and does not touch the tree.
.RE
.sp
After confirmation each update is checked out
.RB ( origin/<branch>
or the tag), the gitlink is staged with
.B git update-index --cacheinfo 160000
.B before
the nested
.B submodule update --init --recursive
so children see the new parent pins,
and a local commit
.B chore: update dependencies
is created if the index is dirty.
There is
.B no push
.
.TP
.B submodules add\fR \fIdir\fR \fIURL\fR \fIpath\fR \fB--name\fR \fIname\fR
Add a submodule
.RB ( git submodule add --name ).
Does not init or update afterwards.
.I path
must be relative to the repo and must not contain
.BR .. .
.B --name
may appear anywhere.
.TP
.B submodules delete\fR \fIdir\fR (\fB--name\fR \fIname\fR | \fB--url\fR \fIurl\fR | \fB--path\fR \fIpath\fR)
Remove the submodule and delete its folder.
Exactly one selector is required.
No commit, no push.
.SS git
.TP
.B git reset\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
.B git reset --hard
and
.B git clean -fd
on the superproject, the same inside submodules
.RB ( foreach --recursive ),
then
.B submodule update --init --recursive
.
.TP
.B git pull\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
.B git fetch origin
and
.B git pull --rebase --no-recurse-submodules ,
then nested modules sync to SHAs
.B already recorded
by the parent.
Does
.B not
re-pin first-level modules.
.TP
.B git sync\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Alias for
.BR "git pull" .
.SS repos
.TP
.B repos list
Non-recursive listing of immediate folders under
.BR ROOT :
folder name, remote, latest tag (or HEAD SHA), current branch.
.TP
.B repos dump\fR \fIdirectory\fR [\fIchunk_size_kb\fR] [\fBtype=\fRc++|\fBtype=\fRcmake]
Dump sources into
.BR OUT
as
.IR project_<name>.txt
(and
.I project_<name>_test.txt
for
.BR type=c++ ).
A numeric argument splits the dump into chunks of that many KiB.
.B type=cmake
collects CMake / template files and skips the test dump.
Excludes
.BR .git ,
.BR build ,
.B thirdparty
and
.BR dist .
.TP
.B repos status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Working tree plus upstream:
.BR OK ,
.BR DIRTY ,
.B UNPUSHED
or
.BR DIRTY+UNPUSHED .
.TP
.B repos push\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
.B git push
(no
.BR --force ).
Skipped if no upstream is configured.
Honours
.BR DRY_RUN .
.TP
.B repos release\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fIversion\fR] [\fB--list\fR | \fB--delete\fR | \fB--skip-ci\fR]
Manage version tags and GitHub Releases for
.B OWNER
repositories.
.RS
.TP
.B --list
List GitHub Releases (not bare tags).
.I dir-spec
and
.I version
are optional.
A lone SEMVER-shaped token is treated as a version filter for every repo
under
.BR ROOT .
Tags that exist without a matching Release are reported as a note, not an
error.
.TP
.B --delete \fIdir version
Remove the GitHub Release and the tag (local and
.BR origin )
after typing exactly
.BR yes .
No-op if neither exists.
.B --skip-ci
is ignored.
.TP
create (default)
.I dir version
[\fB--skip-ci\fR]
Tag, push and create a GitHub Release.
Requires a clean tree on
.B master
or
.BR main ,
an
.B OWNER
remote, and a non-empty
.B CHANGELOG.md
section
.BI "## [" version "] - YYYY-MM-DD" .
Release notes come from that section.
The command waits for CI on HEAD unless
.B --skip-ci
is given
(Ctrl-C during the wait leaves no tag).
The same version deletes and recreates tag and Release.
Pre-releases such as
.B 1.0.0-rc.1
pass
.B --prerelease
to
.BR gh .
Confirmation must be exactly
.BR yes .
.B DRY_RUN=1
is supported for create and delete.
.RE
.SS clone-all
.TP
.B clone-all
Clone every
.B public
repository of
.B OWNER
that is missing under
.BR ROOT .
Existing folders are left alone.
Honours
.BR DRY_RUN .
.SS search
.TP
.B search \fItext\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Search selected clones.
Uses
.BR rg (1)
when available, otherwise
.BR grep (1).
Excludes
.BR .git ,
.BR build ,
.B thirdparty
and
.BR dist .
.SS fork
Uses
.B FORK_ROOT
when set, otherwise
.BR ROOT .
.TP
.B fork status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Behind / ahead versus upstream.
Non-forks are reported and skipped.
.TP
.B fork sync\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Update
.B only
.B master
when the fork is behind upstream.
Refuses if the remote is not a fork.
.TP
.B fork branch-status\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR]
Local branches other than
.BR master :
.B CLEAN
or
.B CONFLICTS
for a merge into
.B master
via
.BR merge-tree .
Notes local-only or origin-divergent tips.
Requires a local
.B master
branch.
.SS test
.TP
.B test asan|tsan\fR [\fIdir-spec\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
Configure, build and run AddressSanitizer or ThreadSanitizer tests.
The same dir-spec rules apply.
.PP
The build directory is created by the script and
.B always
removed on return (success or failure).
If the build directory already exists the repository is skipped for safety.
.PP
Execution priority per repository:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
.B --executable
\(-> run that binary
(relative to the build directory, or absolute).
.IP 2. 3
.B --test
.I REGEX
\(->
.B ctest -R
.IR REGEX .
.IP 3. 3
(none) \(->
.B ctest
(all tests).
.RE
.PP
Options:
.TP
.BI --builddir " DIR"
Build directory relative to the repo root
(default:
.B build-asan
/
.BR build-tsan ).
.TP
.BI --testdir " DIR"
Directory passed to
.B ctest --test-dir
(default:
.IR $builddir/test ).
.TP
.BI --outfile " FILE"
Report file
(default:
.IR /tmp/<repo>_asan|tsan_report.txt ).
Written only when the run fails.
.TP
.BI --cmake-options " opts"
Extra arguments passed to
.B cmake
.B after
the sanitizer flags, so they can override them.
Default extra:
.BR -DENABLE_TEST=ON .
.TP
.BI --executable " PATH"
Run this binary instead of
.BR ctest .
.TP
.BI --test " REGEX"
.B ctest -R
.IR REGEX .
.TP
.BI --asan-options " opts"
Extra
.B ASAN_OPTIONS
.RB ( test asan
only).
.TP
.BI --tsan-options " opts"
Extra
.B TSAN_OPTIONS
.RB ( test tsan
only).
.TP
.B --verbose
Show full configure and compile output.
.SH OUTPUT COLOURS
Section headers stay blue / cyan.
The rest of the CLI uses a short palette:
.TP
dark green
Idle / no work
.RI ( "No changes" ,
.BR OK
with nothing done).
.TP
light green (bold)
A planned or applied update.
.TP
yellow
Warnings
.RB ( DIRTY ,
.BR UNPUSHED ,
unresolved prompts).
.TP
red
Failures,
.BR DIRTY+UNPUSHED ,
.BR CONFLICTS ,
error / UNRESOLVED rows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
StormByte-GitHub help

# Directory selection
StormByte-GitHub repos status
StormByte-GitHub repos status multimedia
StormByte-GitHub repos push '!multimedia'
StormByte-GitHub git sync '!multimedia+!legacy'

# Releases
StormByte-GitHub repos release --list
StormByte-GitHub repos release database --list
StormByte-GitHub repos release --list 1.0.0
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --skip-ci
DRY_RUN=1 StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0
StormByte-GitHub repos release database 1.0.0 --delete

# Fork helpers
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork status
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork sync
FORK_ROOT=~/Forks StormByte-GitHub fork branch-status

# Caches / CI
StormByte-GitHub cache list
StormByte-GitHub cache list --name '*ccache*'
StormByte-GitHub cache show multimedia --name 'sccache-Windows-*'
StormByte-GitHub cache delete '!multimedia'
StormByte-GitHub ci start --failed

# Git / submodules
ROOT=~/Software StormByte-GitHub git sync
StormByte-GitHub submodules update
StormByte-GitHub submodules update database
StormByte-GitHub submodules update database --confirm
DRY_RUN=1 StormByte-GitHub submodules update
StormByte-GitHub submodules list crypto
StormByte-GitHub submodules add database https://github.com/example/lib.git thirdparty/lib --name lib
StormByte-GitHub submodules delete database --name lib

# Search / dump
StormByte-GitHub search "mimalloc"
StormByte-GitHub repos dump ./base type=cmake 200

# Sanitizer tests
StormByte-GitHub test asan
StormByte-GitHub test asan multimedia
StormByte-GitHub test tsan '!multimedia'
StormByte-GitHub test asan database --cmake-options "-DENABLE_FOO=ON" --verbose
StormByte-GitHub test asan multimedia --executable bin/my_test --outfile /tmp/report.txt
StormByte-GitHub test tsan crypto --test "Thread.*"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
(including help, dry-run, and “nothing to do”).
.TP
.B 1
General error
(invalid arguments, missing configuration, git/gh failure, red CI,
aborted confirmation, sanitizer configure/build/run failure,
planner error, ...).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.StormByte-GitHub.conf
Configuration file
.RB ( OWNER ,
.BR ROOT ,
.BR OUT ;
optional
.BR FORK_ROOT ).
.TP
.I functions.sh
Shared helpers (logging, SEMVER, path normalisation, prompts, topological
sort, column printer, ...).
Looked for first next to the script, then in
.IR /lib/StormByte/ .
Required version \(>= 1.3.0.
.TP
.I git.sh
Git-specific helpers, including pin-family tables, shadow refs
.RB ( refs/sb-gh/tags ,
.BR refs/sb-gh/heads )
and
.BR git_sm_plan .
Same search path as
.IR functions.sh .
Required version \(>= 1.3.0.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Repositories must belong to the configured
.B OWNER
(or the
.B OWNER
environment override).
.IP \(bu 2
Omitting the dir-spec walks every immediate subdirectory of the effective
root.
.IP \(bu 2
.B git pull
/
.B git sync
do
.B not
change first-level pin policy; that is
.BR "submodules update" .
.IP \(bu 2
Removing
.B branch=master
from
.I .gitmodules
is the explicit signal for case B2, including an intentional downgrade
onto a release tag.
.IP \(bu 2
.B DRY_RUN=1
is recommended before a bulk
.BR "cache delete" ,
.BR "repos release --delete"
or a wide
.BR "git reset" .
.IP \(bu 2
Running with no arguments shows the built-in help.
